{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.frobenius_gram_matrix","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Archimedean.frobenius_gram_matrix","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Matrix.Symmetric","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Matrix.Notation"],"declarations":4,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.frobenius_gram_matrix","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.frobenius_gram_matrix","kind":"theorem","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/frobenius_gram_matrix.lean#L95-L101","doc":"**Proposition** (statement bundle):\nThe matrix is well-defined and the (0, 0) entry coincides with\n`1` (Markov-trace normalisation). ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:frobenius-gram-matrix","label":"prop:frobenius-gram-matrix","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/frobenius-gram-matrix.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.frobeniusGramMatrix_isSymm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.frobeniusGramMatrix_isSymm","kind":"theorem","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/frobenius_gram_matrix.lean#L83-L93","doc":"**Matrix symmetry**: the Gram matrix is symmetric, reflecting the\nFrobenius-pairing property `tr_M(a · b) = tr_M(b · a)` (Markov-\ntrace cyclicity).\n\nEach off-diagonal pair is identical by construction, so the\nproof is by index-case analysis. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.frobeniusGramMatrix_zero_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.frobeniusGramMatrix_zero_zero","kind":"theorem","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/frobenius_gram_matrix.lean#L74-L81","doc":"**Top-left entry**: `G[0,0] = tr_M(γ · γ) = tr_M(1) = 1`.\n\nThis is the Markov-trace normalisation `tr_M(1) = 1`, recorded\nhere as a direct entry of the matrix. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.frobeniusGramMatrix","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.frobeniusGramMatrix","kind":"def","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/frobenius_gram_matrix.lean#L54-L72","doc":"The Markov–Frobenius `6 × 6` Gram matrix on the NF basis\n`{γ, σ₀, σ₁, L₊, L₋, e⁻}` of `H₃(q)`, parameterised by\n`h = q − q⁻¹` (Hecke parameter) and `z = 1 / (q^{1/2} + q^{−1/2})`\n(Markov parameter).  Entries are polynomial in `h` and `z`.\n\nSee [`prop:frobenius-gram-matrix`] for the categorical\nderivation; entries are read off the Skein decomposition of\neach product `b_i · b_j` plus the Markov-trace evaluation. ","signatureChunk":0}]}